I LOVE MIRIAM (it also helps that it's like a block from our apt) but truly everything is so good. I've been to brunch twice and dinner once and truly everything was so good! Brunch I normally get the herbed eggs but I've also gotten the green shakshuka. I liked the shakshuka but it stays hot for very long in the dish it's in which is great, but harder to eat.

My boyfriend loves the Burekas and we love the labneh cheese and mixing everything together. Service is good and during brunch very fast as they get quite busy. I wouldn't say rushed, but just like woah it's fast.

For dinner, my friend and I split the short ribs and the chicken schnitzel. Short ribs - omg so gooood esp the potatoes it comes with. Chicken schnitzel tasted very good, but was a bit dry and harder to cut.

Overall though one of my favorite park slope places. For brunch, if you can get there close to when they open, you won't have to wait. After 11am it's usually 30+ mins. For dinner during the week, I haven't had to wait


